From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] include, sti: the WIA 1 and 2 interfaces, their proxies, and the WIA dialogs (8300)

include, sti: the WIA 1 and 2 interfaces, their proxies, and the WIA dialogs

include/wia_lh.idl had IWiaDevMgr and the device list only (IWiaItem and
IWiaPropertyStorage were empty "FIXME: fill in" interfaces, WIA 2 was missing):
it now declares WIA 1 (IWiaItem, IEnumWiaItem, IWiaPropertyStorage,
IWiaDataTransfer, IWiaDataCallback, IEnumWIA_FORMAT_INFO, IEnumWIA_DEV_CAPS,
IWiaItemExtras) and WIA 2 (IWiaDevMgr2, CLSID_WiaDevMgr2, IWiaItem2,
IEnumWiaItem2, IWiaTransfer, IWiaTransferCallback, IWiaPreview) with their
structures; include/wiadef.h has every WIA property ID, name, flag, error, format,
category, command and event of the published Windows definitions. sti.dll, the
WIA proxy DLL, builds proxies and stubs for all of them, and also for the
property set interfaces (IEnumSTATPROPSTG and friends had none in Wine), which
IWiaPropertyStorage::Enum returns across the process boundary.

As on Windows the dialogs run in the calling program, with its windows: the
methods that take a window (SelectDeviceDlg, SelectDeviceDlgID, GetImageDlg,
AddDeviceDlg, the items' DeviceDlg) are local to the proxy, which shows the
dialog and talks to the WIA service through the other methods:
- Select Device: the scanners and cameras in a list, manufacturer and
  description, Properties, OK/Cancel (S_FALSE); one device is taken without
  asking unless WIA_SELECT_DEVICE_NODEFAULT; none is WIA_S_NO_DEVICE_AVAILABLE.
- Scan using <device> (WIA 1 DeviceDlg, GetImageDlg): paper source, Color /
  Grayscale / Black and white picture or text / Custom Settings, "Adjust the
  quality of the scanned picture" (Advanced Properties: brightness, contrast,
  resolution, picture type), a preview of the bed with the area to scan,
  Preview / Scan / Cancel; GetImageDlg transfers into the file and format asked.
- New Scan (WIA 2 DeviceDlg, GetImageDlg): profile (Photo, Documents), source
  (flatbed, feeder one or both sides), color format, file type, resolution,
  brightness, contrast, preview; the pages are saved as "name.ext",
  "name (2).ext" ... in the folder given, and their paths returned.
- a progress window with Cancel while the device scans.
The roots and items a program gets (CreateDevice, the item enumerators) carry one
reference more on the program's side, kept until it ends: NAPS2's WIA driver releases
an item and then the same pointer again as its property storage while it still uses
it, which Windows tolerates; here it freed the proxy and NAPS2 crashed in its
finalizers (feeder scans, grayscale).
idtGetData writes a file of the calling program (TYMED_FILE; without a name, a
temporary file whose name is handed back): the proxy makes it and the service
streams the picture into it.
